  "note": "Reflection-first kit, neutral black colourway (Tissot/Casio-style low key). Cards are emissive planes with a linear strength ramp (strength = [start, end] along the card's local Y); they appear only in reflections and as light. Flags are black absorbers. Angles: az 0 = dial normal, negative = viewer's left; el up; distance metres from the dial centre. The crystal mirrors roughly +-35 deg around the camera axis, so only the deliberately soft 'crystal sheen' card and the huge dim 'dial fill' sit there. v1.1: no flag in front of the dial (its reflection read as a dark shape across the crystal). Front-on pose (reference: straight, centred, bracelet running straight up/down and fading into the dark): camera `front_ref` is a long lens straight-on; the vignette ellipse is tall so the bracelet falls off to black top and bottom. v1.1: two cards above/below the camera axis (>= ~25 deg) light the straight bracelet by reflection without veiling the crystal; dial fill dimmed; tall vignette softened. v1.2: bracelet cards tall, ramped (dim toward the camera axis) and heavily feathered.",
